# Check every text file out with LF line endings, on Windows too.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF as
# CRLF on checkout. That changes file bytes, and several build inputs are
# checked byte for byte:
#   - vendor/: Cargo verifies every file against .cargo-checksum.json
#     (SR-29) and refuses to build if one differs;
#   - initramfs/ and the license texts: they are packed into the image
#     and release artifacts, which must be identical on every host (SR-30).
# Attributes in this file override the user's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored crates are third-party bytes: never convert anything in them.
vendor/** -text
